   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyvHf",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I've seen two versions of New Zealand: one where people get ahead, and one where they're barely holding on. I grew up in the second. That gap is why, in a country this prosperous, people are still homeless, jobless and hungry, and it's widened over time. I'm running because I believe everyone deserves the chance to thrive, and no one, least of all our young people, should go without a home or a meal."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyvJq",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I know what it's like to come from a struggling community and family, and that shapes how I'd represent this one. Good representation isn't always about how long you've lived somewhere, it's also about who you listen to and who you fight for. I'd show up for the people growth is leaving behind: young people, renters, working families. I'd bring Labour's commitment to fair work, decent housing and healthcare everyone can reach."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyvM1",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Build the affordable housing our communities need so people aren't priced out of the region."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyvOC",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Make sure health services and staffing keep pace with our growing population."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyvQN",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Back secure local jobs that pay enough to live on, and training pathways for young people."
     }
    ],
