  "description": "Mount Maunganui covers the eastern side of Tauranga and its satellite towns, including Pāpāmoa, Welcome Bay, and Matapihi. The electorate is being contested for the first time in 2026, though its predecessor electorate Bay of Plenty was won by National’s Tom Rutherford in 2023 with a margin of 23,303. Rutherford is standing again in Mount Maunganui. National won the Bay of Plenty party vote with 47% of the vote, followed by Labour on 17%.\n\n",
